pt-oss-120b,qwen/qwen3.6-27b --calls 40\n    python backend/tests/manual/smoke_tool_calling.py --list                # show the probes, spend nothing\n\nWHAT IT ANSWERS: \"which OpenAI-compatible model should M2C use while it is being built?\" It sends 20 real,\nsingle-shot, tool-calling requests (a rotation over 10 probes, twice each) through the real M2C adapter\n(codeagent/adapters/openai_compat.py) with the real P00 tool definitions (protocol/v1/tools/*.json), and prints a\nreport you can read to pick the model. It hits a live provider and spends real quota, so it lives in tests/manual/\nand is never collected by pytest. Based on MiniLocker's bake-off (draft repo 54520a2, backend/minilocker/llm/\nbakeoff.py): same idea (probes, \"usable\" vs \"clean\", a verdict), rewritten for streaming, the P00 tools and this\nrepo's key conventions. No code is imported from that repo.\n\nKEYS. Selected by the environment variables the repo already uses, and loaded from backend/.env if present:\nGROQ_API_KEY[_N], MISTRAL_API_KEY[_N], GEMINI_API_KEY[_N], OPENROUTER_API_KEY[_N], HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY[_N]. With no\nkey set the scri","path":"backend/tests/manual/smoke_tool_calling.py","size":24992,"test":true,"test_count":0},{"binary":false,"blank":46,"code":219,"comment":126,"exports":["BACKOFF_BASE_SECONDS","CASSETTE_DIR","CASSETTE_NAME","MAX_RETRIES","REAL_MANIFEST","my_vcr","pytestmark","test_capability_coverage_classification"],"ext":"py","functions":[{"args":0,"async":false,"cc":1,"cc_deep":1,"code":2,"decorators":[],"doc":false,"end":98,"hash":"09927436d2","kind":"function","loc":2,"name":"_cassette_exists","params":[],"qual":"_cassette_exists","returns":"bool","start":97,"test":false,"visibility":"private"},{"args":2,"async":false,"calls":[["classify_tool_intent","backend/utils/llm_client.py::classify_tool_intent"],["time.sleep",null]],"cc":4,"cc_deep":4,"code":13,"decorators":[],"doc":true,"doc1":"classify_tool_intent() itself is deliberately single-shot / fail-open (see its docstring in utils/llm_client.py) -- a real chat send should never retry-and-block on this.","end":294,"hash":"08c842d702","kind":"function","loc":22,"name":"_classify_with_retries","params":[{"annotation":"str","name":"message"},{"annotation":"list","name":"tools"}],"qual":"_classify_with_retries","returns":"dict[str, Any]","start":273,"test":false,"visibility":"private"},{"args":1,"async":false,"calls":[["os.getenv",null],["os.environ.get",null],["manifest_to_tools","backend/utils/capability_tools.py::manifest_to_tools"],["_classify_with_retries","backend/tests/manual/test_capability_coverage.py::_classify_with_retries"]],"cc":29,"cc_deep":29,"code":67,"decorators":["pytest.mark.skipif(not (os.getenv('GROQ_API_KEY') or _cassette_exists(","my_vcr.use_cassette(CASSETTE_NAME, allow_playback_repeats=True)"],"doc":false,"end":391,"hash":"1664e96595","kind":"function","loc":90,"name":"test_capability_coverage_classification","params":[{"name":"monkeypatch"}],"qual":"test_capability_coverage_classification","start":302,"test":true,"visibility":"public"}],"git":{"added":395,"commits":2,"dates":["2026-08-05","2026-08-25"],"deleted":4,"first":"2026-08-05","last":"2026-08-25"},"lang":"python","lines":391,"module_doc":"tests/manual/test_capability_coverage.py — moved from\nscripts/test_capability_coverage.py (B1 manual-tier migration;\noriginally Notebooks Chat-First refinement, Phase 2 step 2.8:\n\"Test 5-10 phrasings per capability; log misfires.\").\n\nHits a live LLM via utils.llm_client.classify_tool_intent(), so this\nlives in tests/manual/ and is never run in CI -- see pytest.ini's\n`manual` marker.\n\nFIXED as a followup to the B1 migration: TEST_CASES had most of its\ncontent commented out in the original scripts/ version -- only\n\"study_guide\" (5 phrasings) plus the 2 generate_workflow\nregression-check cases were active; the other 7 capability categories\n(clusters, facts, suggested_notes, study_flashcards, study_quiz,\nmindmap, podcast, video_overview) had ZER